3|1|16|0|1|1|Region-locked abilities
3|1|16|1|1|1|Making the game less fun since 2025
3|1|16|2|1|1|lupo:2
3|1|16|4|1|1|0|6|Some abilities in this plando are bound to specific regions or puzzles.\nExiting the area will automatically remove the ability until you come back.\n\nThese pickups look like this:\n*Jump* [<purple>Restricted to (some area)</>]|f=480|instant
9|130|8|9|0|int|3
9|130|16|0|1|2|$Turmoil$
9|130|16|2|1|2|shard:38
9|130|16|4|1|2|0|6|$Turmoil$ greatly reduces the respawn timer for enemies and enables enemies to respawn while Ori is closer than normal.\n\nI strongly recommend having Turmoil equipped at all times, or at least when trying to solve a puzzle involving enemies. If the enemies get stuck in an undesirable position or otherwise die, Turmoil will allow you to reset the puzzle quicker.\n\nKeep in mind that equipping Turmoil once the enemies are already dead @has no effect@.|f=600|instant
3|1|4|17|25|38|1|16|0|1|2|$Turmoil$
3|1|4|17|25|38|1|16|2|1|2|shard:38
3|1|4|17|25|38|1|16|4|1|2|0|6|$Turmoil$ greatly reduces the respawn timer for enemies and enables enemies to respawn while Ori is closer than normal.\n\nI strongly recommend having Turmoil equipped at all times, or at least when trying to solve a puzzle involving enemies. If the enemies get stuck in an undesirable position or otherwise die, Turmoil will allow you to reset the puzzle quicker.\n\nKeep in mind that equipping Turmoil once the enemies are already dead @has no effect@.|f=600|instant
3|1|16|0|1|3|Breakable walls
3|1|16|1|1|3|General purpose\ninformation on\nbreakable walls
3|1|16|2|1|3|grom:1
3|1|16|4|1|3|0|6|All breakable walls have a healthbar. The following enemy attacks will deal damage and break them in most cases.\n\n1. Mantis #stomps#.\n2. Lizard #claw# and #pounce# attacks.\n\nAlmost all breakable floors can be damaged by a Mantis #stomp#. The only exception is the bone bridge in Howl's Den.|f=600|instant
9|131|8|9|0|int|3
9|131|16|0|1|4|$Ultra Bash$
9|131|16|2|1|4|shard:32
9|131|16|4|1|4|0|6|$Ultra Bash$ deals damage to the targets you are bashing.\n\nAfter ultrabashing, during #0.5 seconds#, Ori also gains a damaging aura. When Ori comes into contact with the @hurtbox@ of #most things that have a healthbar#, the Ultra Bash damage will also be applied.\n\n<ls_0.8><s_0.8>It is possible to bash a target without Ultra Bash equipped, and immediately equip it within the first few frames to obtain the damaging aura. While this can help you preserve the HP of whatever you are bashing, this trick is not required for this plando.|f=900|instant
3|1|4|17|25|32|1|16|0|1|4|$Ultra Bash$
3|1|4|17|25|32|1|16|2|1|4|shard:32
3|1|4|17|25|32|1|16|4|1|4|0|6|$Ultra Bash$ deals damage to the targets you are bashing.\n\nAfter ultrabashing, during #0.5 seconds#, Ori also gains a damaging aura. When Ori comes into contact with the @hurtbox@ of #most things that have a healthbar#, the Ultra Bash damage will also be applied.\n\n<ls_0.8><s_0.8>It is possible to bash a target without Ultra Bash equipped, and immediately equip it within the first few frames to obtain the damaging aura. While this can help you preserve the HP of whatever you are bashing, this trick is not required for this plando.|f=900|instant
